  "body": "## What\n\n- Adds the `/sandbox/gym/select` playground route with the Ferrara option list and parameters for label-valued options, duplicates, a disabled option, delayed options, a preselected option, a custom listbox, and dated labels.\n- Adds eleven Gym cases: eight for `session.select@1` and three for `session.legacySelect@1`.\n\n## Why\n\n- Every behavior in the [BE-3483](https://linear.app/sola-ai/issue/BE-3483) decision record gets a case on the real engine path.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The three negative cases (`select-duplicate-different-values`, `select-unknown-value`, `select-custom-widget`) use master's `expectedOutcome` support and only before-action collectors.\n- `select-unknown-value` and `legacy-select-stale-label` separate the two actions: the first returns `noMatchingOption`, the second selects through type-ahead prefix retention on labels dated `2026-04-17 13:52:22.000 CDMX`.\n- `select-custom-widget` targets the widget and expects `notNativeSelect`. The hidden `<select>` behind it is covered by the action integration suites as `notFound`.\n- Shared Gym runner, schema, and adapters are unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\nAll eleven select cases compile alongside the existing cases, after the restack onto master `079e044d0c`. Engine runs are not part of this output. Listing trimmed to the select cases.\n\n```text\n$ tsx --conditions=development src/suites/gym/cli.ts --check\nlegacy-select-by-label: compiled (not executed)\nlegacy-select-custom-widget: compiled (not executed)\nlegacy-select-stale-label: compiled (not executed)\nselect-by-label: compiled (not executed)\nselect-by-value-fallback: compiled (not executed)\nselect-custom-widget: compiled (not executed)\nselect-duplicate-different-values: compiled (not executed)\nselect-duplicate-same-value: compiled (not executed)\nselect-folded-label: compiled (not executed)\nselect-options-after-delay: compiled (not executed)\nselect-unknown-value: compiled (not executed)\n```\n\n- Gym engine runs of the eleven cases on Selenium and Playwright pending, Cory runs them once the shared ports are free.\n",
